WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.570
Morning, John

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:06.000
I am a bit worn out on philosophical musings and to tell you the truth, a bit worn out in general.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.480
Planning conferences is hard.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:11.880
So today, instead of thinking too much about things that people usually don't think very much about,

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:15.000
I'm just gonna tell you the fascinating tale of Phineas Gage.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.480
In 1848, Phineas Gage was a hard-working, well-liked construction foreman working on the railroad.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:24.420
He was helping to blow up the side of a mountain so that they could run a railroad through it.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:25.880
And this is something he'd been doing for quite a long time.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.960
You drill a hole into a rock and you put some blasting powder in there

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.100
and then you put some sand in there to pack it down,

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.880
then you pack it down with this rock.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:33.680
So Phineas was doing this

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:35.020
and then someone distracted him.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:36.707
And I don't know what it was, the distraction.

00:00:36.707 --> 00:00:37.590
Maybe it was a raccoon,

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.040
maybe it was a hot girl walking down the railway.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.120
But when Phineas came back to his work,

00:00:41.129 --> 00:00:43.440
he did not realize that he had not put the sand in,

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.220
and so he shoved his little rod down the hole,

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:47.400
creating a spark,

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.260
and the blasting powder ignited

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.920
and his iron rod landed EIGHTY FEET AWAY.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:55.880
Unfortunately, there was something in between that hole and whatever it was that was 80 feet away

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:56.850
and that thing

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.280
was Phineas Gage's head.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:00.840
The rod went through about, about here

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:02.480
and came out like here.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.500
And now, those of you who do not know this story are expecting the story to end,

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.880
because where could the story go from there?

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:08.380
Well,

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:10.540
three minutes later, Phineas Gage regained consciousness,

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:11.840
started talking to people,

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.200
walked over to a cart,

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.220
got in the cart,

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:17.480
sat up for the three-quarter mile travel back to his house,

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:20.940
waited there for a doctor and then, when the doctor finally got there,

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.480
they chatted about it.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:24.320
The doctor took some wonderful written notes,

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.760
which we have copies of and I'm going to share some of that with you,

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:29.180
though you may not want to listen if you're a little bit squeamish.

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:30.220
The doctor wrote,

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:33.120
"I did not believe Mr. Gage's statement at the time,

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:34.560
but thought he was deceived.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:38.280
Mr. Gage persisted in saying that the rod went through his head.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.900
Mr. Gage got up and vomited,

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:41.920
the effort of the vomiting pushed out about

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:43.200
half a teacupful of brain,

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.680
which fell onto the floor."

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:49.480
The unit of measurement "teacupful" has- has since fallen out of use but, but, it's roughly--

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:51.340
WAY TOO MUCH BRAIN.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:55.360
At that same visit Phineas said to the doctor that he hoped he wasn't much hurt.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:57.780
To which the doctor presumably replied,

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:58.900
"uhhh."

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:02.680
In the coming weeks, Gage would drop in and out of a coma caused by hemorrhaging in his brain.

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:08.800
His family was assured that there was no possible way that he could live, which is also backed up by,

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:09.680
y'know, reason,

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:11.980
and they had his coffin and his burial clothes all ready

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:14.120
and then, two months after the accident,

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:16.340
Phineas Gage was walking around,

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:17.540
talking,

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:19.220
basically a normal guy.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:20.680
He wasn't quite normal,

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:23.760
he wasn't quite the Phineas Gage that everyone had come to know and love,

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.360
but on the whole, a lot healthier than you would expect from a guy who had lost

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:29.700
several teacupfuls of brain.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:33.080
So because of his behavioral problems, Phineas Gage did lose his construction job,

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:35.460
but PT Barnum, not to miss a weirdo,

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:36.980
found this guy and his iron rod and

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:39.700
Phineas did a little tour of the circuses, earning some money that way.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:41.589
His psychological problems began to subside.

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:42.880
He started holding down good jobs.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:46.280
And eventually, he moved to Chile to become a long-distance stagecoach driver,

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:49.220
in a place where people didn't know that he was Phineas Gage.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:52.180
Twelve years after the accident, late-onset epilepsy set in,

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:54.780
which is very common in these kinds of injuries,

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:57.680
and Phineas's health declined until he finally died.

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:00.620
But the man had a three and a half foot long rod of iron

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:01.420
pass through his head

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:03.440
at hundreds of miles per hour.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.960
And he was pretty much okay for twelve years.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:07.840
A final footnote to this bizarre tale:

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:12.720
In 2009, a couple, who loved to collect old photographs of people,

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:16.120
were scanning their collection and uploading it to the photo-sharing website, flickr.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:18.280
They uploaded a picture that they called, "The Whaler",

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:21.080
thinking that it was an injured whaler with his harpoon.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:26.259
Flickr quickly told them that there was no way that that big shaft of iron was any kind of harpoon.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.560
But no one had any suggestions about what else it could be,

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.340
until somebody commented, saying,

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:33.140
"You know, you may have a picture of Phineas Gage there,

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:34.340
and if you do

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:37.340
It's the only picture of Phineas Gage that exists."

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:40.280
And that's one more reason why I love the internet!

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.340
Because it was the only picture of Phineas Gage.

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:44.160
So John,

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.140
BEHOLD

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:46.060
Phineas Gage,

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:51.320
the only man to have ever had an iron rod passed through his skull at hundreds of miles per hour,

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:53.420
and live to tell the tale.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.380
I'll see you on Wednesday.

